# 1️⃣ What is a Binary Search Tree?

A Binary Search Tree is a Binary Tree where each node follows the BST ordering property.

Example:

```text
          8
        /   \
       5     12
      / \    / \
     3   7  10  15
```

For node `8`:

```text
Left Subtree  → values smaller than 8

Right Subtree → values greater than 8
```

For node `5`:

```text
Left  → 3
Right → 7
```

The same property must hold recursively for every node.

---

# 2️⃣ BST Property

The most important rule is:

```text
Left Subtree < Root < Right Subtree
```

Example:

```text
          10
        /    \
       5      15
      / \    /  \
     2   7  12  20
```

All values on the left of `10` are smaller than `10`.

All values on the right of `10` are greater than `10`.

---

# 3️⃣ Binary Tree vs BST

| Feature | Binary Tree | BST |
|---------|-------------|-----|
| Maximum Children | 2 | 2 |
| Ordering Rule | No fixed ordering | Left < Root < Right |
| Searching | O(n) | O(h) average |
| Insertion | Depends on implementation | O(h) |
| Inorder Traversal | Not necessarily sorted | Sorted order |

Where:

```text
n = Number of Nodes

h = Height of Tree
```

