# 5️⃣ Search in BST

## 📖 Problem

Given a BST and a target value, determine whether the value exists in the tree.

Example:

```text
          8
        /   \
       5     12
      / \    / \
     3   7  10  15
```

Search:

```text
7
```

---

## 💡 Approach

At every node:

### If:

```text
target == root->data
```

We found the value.

### If:

```text
target < root->data
```

Search the left subtree.

### If:

```text
target > root->data
```

Search the right subtree.

---

### C++ Code - Recursive

```cpp
bool searchBST(Node* root, int target)
{
    if(root == NULL)
        return false;

    if(root->data == target)
        return true;

    if(target < root->data)
        return searchBST(root->left, target);

    return searchBST(root->right, target);
}
```

---

# 6️⃣ Search in BST - Iterative

We can also search without recursion.

### C++ Code

```cpp
bool searchBST(Node* root, int target)
{
    while(root != NULL)
    {
        if(root->data == target)
            return true;

        if(target < root->data)
            root = root->left;
        else
            root = root->right;
    }

    return false;
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Average Time: O(log n)

Worst Time: O(n)

Space: O(1) for iterative approach
```

