# 7️⃣ Insert into BST

## 📖 Problem

Insert a new value while maintaining the BST property.

Example:

Insert:

```text
6
```

Into:

```text
          8
        /   \
       5     12
      / \
     3   7
```

Result:

```text
          8
        /   \
       5     12
      / \
     3   7
        /
       6
```

---

## 💡 Approach

Compare the new value with the current node.

```text
value < root
→ Go Left

value > root
→ Go Right
```

When a NULL position is found:

```text
Create New Node
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
Node* insertBST(Node* root, int value)
{
    if(root == NULL)
        return new Node(value);

    if(value < root->data)
    {
        root->left =
            insertBST(root->left, value);
    }
    else if(value > root->data)
    {
        root->right =
            insertBST(root->right, value);
    }

    return root;
}
```

> The duplicate-value policy depends on the problem. This implementation ignores duplicates.

