# 8️⃣ Find Minimum Value in BST

## 💡 Important Property

The smallest value in a BST is always the **leftmost node**.

Example:

```text
          8
        /   \
       5     12
      /
     3
    /
   1
```

Minimum:

```text
1
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
int findMin(Node* root)
{
    if(root == NULL)
        return -1;

    while(root->left != NULL)
    {
        root = root->left;
    }

    return root->data;
}
```

---

# 9️⃣ Find Maximum Value in BST

The largest value in a BST is always the **rightmost node**.

Example:

```text
          8
        /   \
       5     12
            /  \
           10   15
                  \
                   20
```

Maximum:

```text
20
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
int findMax(Node* root)
{
    if(root == NULL)
        return -1;

    while(root->right != NULL)
    {
        root = root->right;
    }

    return root->data;
}
```

