# 💡 Interview Tips

✅ Remember the main BST rule:

```text
LEFT < ROOT < RIGHT
```

✅ Inorder traversal of a BST gives sorted order.

✅ Minimum = leftmost node.

✅ Maximum = rightmost node.

✅ Searching uses the BST property to eliminate half of the tree at each step in a balanced BST.

✅ Always consider the worst case when discussing BST complexity.

---

# ⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Assuming every Binary Tree is a BST.

❌ Searching both subtrees in a BST unnecessarily.

❌ Forgetting that inorder traversal is sorted only when the tree satisfies the BST property.

❌ Assuming BST operations are always O(log n).

❌ Ignoring the possibility of a skewed BST.

❌ Not considering how duplicates are handled.

